{
  "title": "32: al-Sajdah السجدة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nالٓمّٓ‏(1)\nALIF LAAAM MEEM.\nA. L. M. \nۚ تَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ مِنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(2)\nTANZEELU KETAABE LAA RAYBA FEEHE MIN RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\n(This is) the Revelation of the Book in which there is no doubt, from the Lord of the Worlds. \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ‌ۚ بَلْ هُوَ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لِتُنْذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّاۤ اَتٰٮهُمْ مِّنْ نَّذِيْرٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(3)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU BAL HOWA HAQQO MIN RABBEKA LETUNZERA QAWMAN MAA ATAAHUM MIN NAZEERIM MIN QABLEKA LA-A’LLAHUM YAHTADOON.\nOr do they say, “He has forged it”? Nay, it is the Truth from thy Lord, that thou mayest admonish a people to whom no warner has come before thee: in order that they may receive guidance. \nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ‌ؕ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٍ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(4)\nALLAAHO LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL AL-A’ARSHE MAA LAKUM MIN DOONEHI MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA SHAFEEA’IN AFALAA TATAZAKKAROONA.\nIt is Allah Who has created the heavens and the earth, and all between them, in six Days, and is firmly established on the Throne (of Authority): ye have none, besides Him, to protect or intercede (for you): will ye not then receive admonition? \nيُدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ ثُمَّ يَعْرُجُ اِلَيْهِ فِىْ يَوْمٍ كَانَ مِقْدَارُهٗۤ اَلْفَ سَنَةٍ مِّمَّا تَعُدُّوْنَ‏(5)\nYUDABBERU AMRA MENAL SAMAAA-E ELAL ARZE SUMMA YAA’RUJU ELAYHE FEE YAWMIN KAANA MEQDAARUH AALFA WA MIMMAA TAU’UDDOONA.\nHe rules (all) affairs from the heavens to the earth: in the end will (all affairs) go up to Him, on a Day, the space whereof will be (as) a thousand years of your reckoning. \nذٰلِكَ عٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُۙ‏(6)\nZAALEKA A’ALEMUL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nSuch is He, the Knower of all things, hidden and open, the Exalted (in power), the Merciful;- \nالَّذِىْۤ اَحْسَنَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقَهٗ‌ وَبَدَاَ خَلْقَ الْاِنْسَانِ مِنْ طِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(7)\nLAZEE AHSANAL KULLA SHAY-IN KHALAQAHU WABADAA KHALQA INSAANE MIN TEENIN.\nHe Who has made everything which He has created most good: He began the creation of man with (nothing more than) clay, \nثُمَّ جَعَلَ نَسْلَهٗ مِنْ سُلٰلَةٍ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ مَّهِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(8)\nSUMMA JA-A’LA NASLAH MIN SULAALATIN MIN MAAA-IN MMAHEENIN.\nAnd made his progeny from a quintessence of the nature of a fluid despised: \nثُمَّ سَوّٰٮهُ وَنَفَخَ فِيْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِهٖ‌ وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ ‌ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(9)\nSUMMA SAWHU WANAFAKHA FEEHE MIN RROOHEH WA LAKOMUL JA-A’LA LAKOMUS SAM-A’ WA ABSAARA WAL QALEELAA MAA TASHKOROON.\nBut He fashioned him in due proportion, and breathed into him something of His spirit. And He gave you (the faculties of) hearing and sight and feeling (and understanding): little thanks do ye give! \nوَقَالُوْٓا ءَاِذَا ضَلَلْنَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ءَاِنَّا لَفِىْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍ ؕ ‌بَلْ هُمْ بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّهِمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(10)\nWA A-TAJ-A’LO A-EZAA ZALALNAA FIL ARZE A-INNAA LAFEE KHALQIN JADEEDIN BAL HUM BELEQAAE RABBEHIM KAAFEROON.\nAnd they say: “What! when we lie, hidden and lost, in the earth, shall we indeed be in a Creation renewed? Nay, they deny the Meeting with their Lord. \nقُلْ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ مَّلَكُ الْمَوْتِ الَّذِىْ وُكِّلَ بِكُمْ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(11)\nQUL YATAWAFFAAKUM MMALAKU MAWT LAZEE WUKKELA BEKUM SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM TURJA-O’ON.\nSay: “The Angel of Death, put in charge of you, will (duly) take your souls: then shall ye be brought back to your Lord.” \nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذِ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ نَاكِسُوْا رُءُوْسِهِمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ رَبَّنَاۤ اَبْصَرْنَا وَسَمِعْنَا فَارْجِعْنَا نَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا اِنَّا مُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA LAW TARAAA EZIM MUJREMOON NAAKESOOA RUOOSEHEM I’NDAL RABBEHIM RABBANAA AABSARNAA WA SAMEA’NAA FAARJEA’NAA NAA’MAL SAALEHAN INNAA MOOQENOONA.\nIf only thou couldst see when the guilty ones will bend low their heads before their Lord, (saying:) “Our Lord! We have seen and we have heard: Now then send us back (to the world): we will work righteousness: for we do indeed (now) believe.” \nوَ لَوْ شِئْنَا لَاٰتَيْنَا كُلَّ نَفْسٍ هُدٰٮهَا وَلٰكِنْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ مِنِّىْ لَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَالنَّاسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(13)\nWA LAW SHE’NAA LAATAYNAA KULLA NAFSIM HUDAAHAA WA LAAKIL HAQQA QAWLO MINNEE LAAMLAANNA JAHANNAMA MENAL JINNATE WAN NAASE AJMA-E’ENA.\nIf We had so willed, We could certainly have brought every soul its true guidance: but the Word from Me will come true, “I will fill Hell with Jinns and men all together.” \nفَذُوْقُوْا بِمَا نَسِيْتُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا‌ ۚ اِنَّا نَسِيْنٰكُمْ‌ وَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْخُلْدِ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(14)\nFA-ZOOQOO BEMAA NASEETUM LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEKUM HAAZAA INNAA NASEENAAKUM WA ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL AL-KHULDE BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n“Taste ye then - for ye forgot the Meeting of this Day of yours, and We too will forget you - taste ye the Penalty of Eternity for your (evil) deeds!” \nاِنَّمَا يُؤْمِنُ بِاٰيٰتِنَا الَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهَا خَرُّوْا سُجَّدًا وَّسَبَّحُوْا بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ۩‏(15)\nINNAMAA BIL LAAHE BE-AAYAATENAA LAZEENA EZAA ZUKKEROOA BEHAA KHARROOA SUJJADANW WWASABBAHOOA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WA HUM LAA YASTAKBEROONA.\nOnly those believe in Our Signs, who, when they are recited to them, fall down in prostration, and celebrate the praises of their Lord, nor are they (ever) puffed up with pride. [[۩]] \nتَتَجَافٰى جُنُوْبُهُمْ عَنِ الْمَضَاجِعِ يَدْعُوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ خَوْفًا وَّطَمَعًا وَّمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‏(16)\nTATAJAAFAA JUNOOBUHUM A’NIL AL-MAZAAJEE’E YAD-O’ONA RABBAHUM BARQA KHAWFANW WWAMEMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOONA.\nTheir limbs do forsake their beds of sleep, the while they call on their Lord, in Fear and Hope: and they spend (in charity) out of the sustenance which We have bestowed on them. \nفَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَّاۤ اُخْفِىَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ قُرَّةِ اَعْيُنٍ‌ۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(17)\nFALAA TAA’LAMU NAFSUN MAA AUKHFEAAA LAHUM MIN QURRATE AAA’YUNIN JA-ZAAA-AWN BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nNow no person knows what delights of the eye are kept hidden (in reserve) for them - as a reward for their (good) deeds. \nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ مُؤْمِنًا كَمَنْ كَانَ فَاسِقًا‌ ؕ لَا يَسْتَوٗنَؔ‏(18)\nAFAMAWN KAANA MUMENAN KAMAM KAANA FAASEQAN LAA YASTAWNA.\nIs then the man who believes no better than the man who is rebellious and wicked? Not equal are they. \nاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَلَهُمْ جَنّٰتُ الْمَاْوٰى نُزُلًاۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(19)\nAMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FALAHUM JANNAATU AL-MAAWAA NOZOLAM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nFor those who believe and do righteous deeds are Gardens as hospitable homes, for their (good) deeds. \nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ فَسَقُوْا فَمَاْوٰٮهُمُ النَّارُ‌ؕ كُلَّمَاۤ اَرَادُوْۤا اَنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَاۤ اُعِيْدُوْا فِيْهَا وَ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ ذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ النَّارِ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(20)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA FASAQOOA FAMAAWAAHUMU AN-NAARU KULLAMAA AARAADOOA AN YAKHROJOO MINHAA AUE’EEDOOA FEEHAA WA QEELA LAHUM ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL NAAR LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\nAs to those who are rebellious and wicked, their abode will be the Fire: every time they wish to get away therefrom, they will be forced thereinto, and it will be said to them: “Taste ye the Penalty of the Fire, the which ye were wont to reject as false.” \nوَلَنُذِيْقَنَّهُمْ مِّنَ الْعَذَابِ الْاَدْنٰى دُوْنَ الْعَذَابِ الْاَكْبَرِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA LANOZEEQANNAHUM MENAL A’ZAABE AL-AADNAA DOONA A’ZAABE AL-AAKBARE LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd indeed We will make them taste of the Penalty of this (life) prior to the supreme Penalty, in order that they may (repent and) return. \nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ ذُكِّرَ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهٖ ثُمَّ اَعْرَضَ عَنْهَا‌ؕ اِنَّا مِنَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ مُنْتَقِمُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMAN ZUKKERA BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHI SUMMA A-A’RAZA A’ANHAA INNAA MENAL MUJREMEEN MUNTAQEMOON.\nAnd who does more wrong than one to whom are recited the Signs of his Lord, and who then turns away therefrom? Verily from those who transgress We shall exact (due) Retribution. \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ فَلَا تَكُنْ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْ لِّقَآئِهٖ‌ وَجَعَلْنٰهُ هُدًى لِّبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَۚ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA FALAA TAKUN FEE MIRYATIM MIN LLEQAAEH WA LAW HODAM LLEBANEAA ISRAAA-EELAZ.\nWe did indeed aforetime give the Book to Moses: be not then in doubt of its reaching (thee): and We made it a guide to the Children of Israel. \nوَ جَعَلْنَا مِنْهُمْ اَئِمَّةً يَّهْدُوْنَ بِاَمْرِنَا لَمَّا صَبَرُوْا‌ ؕ وَ كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(24)\nWA JA-A’LNAA MINHUM AIMMATAWN YYAHDOONA BEAAMRENAA LAMMAA SABAROO WA KAANOO BE-AAYAATENAA YOOQENOON.\nAnd We appointed, from among them, leaders, giving guidance under Our command, so long as they persevered with patience and continued to have faith in Our Signs. \nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(25)\nINNAL RABBAKA HOWA YAFSELU BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nVerily thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Judgment, in the matters wherein they differ (among themselves) \nاَوَلَمْ يَهْدِ لَهُمْ كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنَ الْقُرُوْنِ يَمْشُوْنَ فِىْ مَسٰكِنِهِمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ ؕ اَفَلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(26)\nAWALAM YAHDE LAHUM KAM AHLAKNAL MIN QABLEHIM MENAL QOROONE YAMSHOONA FEE MASAAKENEHEM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL AFALAA YAS-MA-O’ONA.\nDoes it not teach them a lesson, how many generations We destroyed before them, in whose dwellings they (now) go to and fro? Verily in that are Signs: Do they not then listen? \nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا نَسُوْقُ الْمَآءَ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ الْجُرُزِ فَنُخْرِجُ بِهٖ زَرْعًا تَاْكُلُ مِنْهُ اَنْعَامُهُمْ وَاَنْفُسُهُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(27)\nAWALAM YARAW ANNAA NASOOQU MAAA-AH ELAL ARZE AL-JURUZE FANUKHREJU BEHI ZARA’AN TAAKULU MINHO AANA’AAMUHUM WAANFUSUHUM AFALAA YUBSEROON.\nAnd do they not see that We do drive rain to parched soil (bare of herbage), and produce therewith crops, providing food for their cattle and themselves? Have they not the vision? \nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْفَتْحُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(28)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAA AL-FATHU IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThey say: “When will this decision be, if ye are telling the truth?” \nقُلْ يَوْمَ الْفَتْحِ لَا يَنْفَعُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِيْمَانُهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(29)\nQUL YAWMA AL-FATHE LAA YANFAU’N LAZEENA KAFAROO AEEMAANUHUM WA LAA HUM HUM YUNZAROON.\nSay: “On the Day of Decision, no profit will it be to Unbelievers if they (then) believe! nor will they be granted a respite.” \nفَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَانْتَظِرْ اِنَّهُمْ مُّنْتَظِرُوْنَ‏(30)\nFAAA’REZ A’NHUM WAANTAZER INNAHUM MMUNTAZEROONA.\nSo turn away from them, and wait: they too are waiting. ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Sajdah (The Adoration)\nThere are 30 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. Some scholars say that the 19th, 20th and 21st verses of this Surah are ‘Madani’. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting Surah al-Sajdah and [Surah al-Mulk](A71) is the same as what reward is gotten if one spends the entire night of Qadr in worship. It is said that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) used to recite these Surahs before sleeping.\nThe person who recites this Surah will be given 60 rewards, forgiven 60 sins and raised 60 levels nearer to Allah (s.w.t.). Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that one who recites this Surah will be given his book of deeds in his right hand on the Day of Judgement and will be counted from among the friends of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and his family. Keeping this Surah in writing works as a cure from aches and pains."
}
